WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.254 --> 00:00:03.337
(instrumental music)

00:00:06.234 --> 00:00:08.393
- My mom had just taken me
on this great shopping spree

00:00:08.393 --> 00:00:09.976
for my birthday, and I
bought these clothes.

00:00:09.976 --> 00:00:11.198
I walked into the lunch room,

00:00:11.198 --> 00:00:13.368
and everyone made so much fun of me.

00:00:13.368 --> 00:00:15.879
I felt so ashamed, the
fact that I was different.

00:00:15.879 --> 00:00:17.973
There are just so many specifics
that have stuck with me

00:00:17.973 --> 00:00:20.205
to this day that have
really instilled the sense

00:00:20.205 --> 00:00:21.460
of, like, fear.

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:23.029
- I had a Pocahontas backpack,

00:00:23.029 --> 00:00:24.814
and I loved that Pocahontas backpack.

00:00:24.814 --> 00:00:26.503
I wore it to school and got ripped,

00:00:26.503 --> 00:00:27.914
and everyone made fun of me.

00:00:27.914 --> 00:00:30.287
It just became a routine
where I would come home

00:00:30.287 --> 00:00:31.979
from elementary school crying.

00:00:31.979 --> 00:00:33.814
- I was teased growing up for being gay

00:00:33.814 --> 00:00:35.378
before I even knew that I was gay.

00:00:35.378 --> 00:00:37.625
Fourth grade, only played
with girls at recess,

00:00:37.625 --> 00:00:39.997
and my teacher took me out of class

00:00:39.997 --> 00:00:41.016
and talked to me and was like,

00:00:41.016 --> 00:00:43.332
"You should really hang out
with other boys sometimes."

00:00:43.332 --> 00:00:45.653
And I remember being like,
"Why are you telling me

00:00:45.653 --> 00:00:47.648
"who I should hang out with
and why does it matter?"

00:00:47.648 --> 00:00:49.856
- Growing up in elementary, I
always hung out with the girls

00:00:49.856 --> 00:00:51.422
but I did actually like them at that time.

00:00:51.422 --> 00:00:52.927
I had a crush on like almost every girl

00:00:52.927 --> 00:00:53.961
at the table I sat with at one point.

00:00:53.961 --> 00:00:55.119
They're like, oh I just
see you as a friend.

00:00:55.119 --> 00:00:55.952
- (laughing) Awe. That's
the saddest thing.

00:00:55.952 --> 00:00:59.679
- But I remember the jock
guys always telling me like,

00:00:59.679 --> 00:01:01.695
oh you're gay, and like, (bleeping) gay,

00:01:01.695 --> 00:01:03.142
and people making fun of me not only

00:01:03.142 --> 00:01:05.342
cause they assumed I was gay,
but because I was overweight.

00:01:05.342 --> 00:01:08.182
- I was asked, growing up, like if I was,

00:01:08.182 --> 00:01:10.233
and I was like, oh my god,
are they going to find out?

00:01:10.233 --> 00:01:11.507
Growing up, you hear stories

00:01:11.507 --> 00:01:12.874
about gay people getting
killed on the street.

00:01:12.874 --> 00:01:14.901
- And that like happens still now.

00:01:14.901 --> 00:01:15.734
- Yeah

00:01:15.734 --> 00:01:16.567
- Which is horrifying.

00:01:16.567 --> 00:01:19.010
- I was bullied in middle school

00:01:19.010 --> 00:01:22.026
by somebody who eventually came out,

00:01:22.026 --> 00:01:23.631
and he would bully me for being gay

00:01:23.631 --> 00:01:27.229
which was him projecting
onto me his insecurities.

00:01:27.229 --> 00:01:29.612
- I think being bullied
for being gay just kind

00:01:29.612 --> 00:01:32.278
of confirmed that I didn't
want to come out of the closet.

00:01:32.278 --> 00:01:34.736
I was afraid of coming out
and admitting to myself,

00:01:34.736 --> 00:01:36.376
and to the world, like who I really am.

00:01:36.376 --> 00:01:39.025
- I don't know if that
kind of trickled down

00:01:39.025 --> 00:01:40.343
into like my adulthood.

00:01:40.343 --> 00:01:43.267
Now, I am sure it has cause
everything that we experience

00:01:43.267 --> 00:01:45.693
in our lives like affects
us in one way or another.

00:01:45.693 --> 00:01:48.750
(light instrumental music)

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:50.506
- I don't show PDA when I'm on the street,

00:01:50.506 --> 00:01:51.587
like I don't hold hands.

00:01:51.587 --> 00:01:53.819
I'm afraid that society
is going to regress,

00:01:53.819 --> 00:01:55.439
and then all of a sudden there's gonna

00:01:55.439 --> 00:01:56.740
to be laws about being gay.

00:01:56.740 --> 00:01:57.721
- Gay people are getting shot,

00:01:57.721 --> 00:01:58.920
gay people are getting, like, attacked.

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:01.570
Oh, it's okay to hate
people who aren't like you.

00:02:01.570 --> 00:02:04.272
I definitely do feel like
already a shift back.

00:02:04.272 --> 00:02:06.672
I still haven't let it
overwhelm me with fear yet,

00:02:06.672 --> 00:02:08.460
but it is like this
little thing nagging me

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:09.293
in the back of my head, like,

00:02:09.293 --> 00:02:11.424
"Is it still okay for you
to be yourself all the time?

00:02:11.424 --> 00:02:13.830
"Are you going to getting
a rock thrown at your head

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:15.907
"if you like hold your boyfriend's hand?"

00:02:15.907 --> 00:02:18.207
- I think for me the
biggest fear that I have is

00:02:18.207 --> 00:02:20.639
that the younger generation
kind of coming up people

00:02:20.639 --> 00:02:23.111
in their teens and 20s
have had it pretty good,

00:02:23.111 --> 00:02:25.623
like, they've seen so much
change in the past 10 years,

00:02:25.623 --> 00:02:28.824
and where being gay is very
accepted and almost a norm

00:02:28.824 --> 00:02:31.906
in society, and they don't
know how hard it has been

00:02:31.906 --> 00:02:33.303
to fight for those things.

00:02:33.303 --> 00:02:35.157
Some of those rights
can still be taken away.

00:02:35.157 --> 00:02:36.945
- And they are, even me,
like, the difference,

00:02:36.945 --> 00:02:39.206
I know it's not a big age
difference, but there's a lot

00:02:39.206 --> 00:02:41.777
of very privileged gay
kids growing up now.

00:02:41.777 --> 00:02:42.610
You could literally tell them,

00:02:42.610 --> 00:02:44.180
"Oh, well this person
helped with this movement."

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:45.290
And they'll be like, "Oh I
don't care, blah, blah, blah."

00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:47.531
And ya know, they should
because that's the reason why

00:02:47.531 --> 00:02:50.015
they can be so IDGAF on Instagram

00:02:50.015 --> 00:02:51.858
and, I don't care haters,
and this and that,

00:02:51.858 --> 00:02:54.043
because of people like that
that have fought for me.

00:02:54.043 --> 00:02:55.950
- For me, especially, it felt like,

00:02:55.950 --> 00:02:57.469
you're not accepted, you're
gay, you're gay, you're gay,

00:02:57.469 --> 00:02:59.324
and then all the sudden,
wow, gays can get married,

00:02:59.324 --> 00:03:00.557
it's cool again.

00:03:00.557 --> 00:03:02.376
We forget about the middle of the country,

00:03:02.376 --> 00:03:05.764
and the students out there
who can't be protected,

00:03:05.764 --> 00:03:07.345
and I think that there's
still a lot of work to do,

00:03:07.345 --> 00:03:09.334
starting to be more mindful of the laws

00:03:09.334 --> 00:03:11.064
that protect people like me

00:03:11.064 --> 00:03:13.775
and little kids out there who need it.

00:03:13.775 --> 00:03:16.922
(ambient music)

00:03:16.922 --> 00:03:18.086
- I think when I first
came out, I was like,

00:03:18.086 --> 00:03:20.195
"Oh yeah, it would be a lot
easier if I were straight."

00:03:20.195 --> 00:03:21.987
- I have never wished I was straight.

00:03:21.987 --> 00:03:24.017
- I remember going to sleep
sometimes, and being like,

00:03:24.017 --> 00:03:26.482
"Oh, man, I wish I was straight,
I wish I was straight."

00:03:26.482 --> 00:03:27.913
And then crying and
everything, it was intense.

00:03:27.913 --> 00:03:29.648
- When I met my current boyfriend,

00:03:29.648 --> 00:03:31.852
I told him that one day
I would marry a girl

00:03:31.852 --> 00:03:33.859
cause at the time I was not out at all,

00:03:33.859 --> 00:03:36.206
and that's what I thought I had to do.

00:03:36.206 --> 00:03:37.466
That's what society tells you,

00:03:37.466 --> 00:03:39.845
please my parents, deny
a big part of myself.

00:03:39.845 --> 00:03:43.224
Now I love being gay
because that's who I am.

00:03:43.224 --> 00:03:45.787
- No, no I never wished
I was straight, never.

00:03:45.787 --> 00:03:47.375
- I absolutely did wish I was straight.

00:03:47.375 --> 00:03:48.927
I thought, when I was younger,

00:03:48.927 --> 00:03:52.366
that being gay would mean
a life of more bullying.

00:03:52.366 --> 00:03:53.818
- As much bullying as I went through,

00:03:53.818 --> 00:03:56.624
and had to like endure, being
gay has become something

00:03:56.624 --> 00:03:58.348
that I am so, so, so proud of.

00:03:58.348 --> 00:04:00.063
- But once you like rip that Band-Aid off,

00:04:00.063 --> 00:04:01.846
you're out, no I wouldn't change a thing.

00:04:01.846 --> 00:04:04.070
- You come out of the closet
and you just seal that door.

00:04:04.070 --> 00:04:05.695
- (laughing) Yep.

00:04:05.695 --> 00:04:07.462
- But a lot of the time, I like forget

00:04:07.462 --> 00:04:09.600
that being gay is seen
as the abnormal thing

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:11.042
because it's just like what my life is

00:04:11.042 --> 00:04:12.392
and how I love living my life,

00:04:12.392 --> 00:04:13.225
and everyone has told me like,

00:04:13.225 --> 00:04:14.732
wouldn't it suck if I was straight?

00:04:14.732 --> 00:04:16.235
Cause then I wouldn't
have all this like great,

00:04:16.235 --> 00:04:17.286
gay sex, like...

00:04:17.286 --> 00:04:18.119
(laughing)

00:04:18.119 --> 00:04:19.917
- I don't know, like, I'm so creative,

00:04:19.917 --> 00:04:21.222
and I love making people laugh.

00:04:21.222 --> 00:04:22.409
The whole like creative aspect,

00:04:22.409 --> 00:04:23.699
I've opened and let blossom

00:04:23.699 --> 00:04:25.172
because I was honest with myself.

00:04:25.172 --> 00:04:27.630
- Now that I'm gay, and I
see how fucking great it is,

00:04:27.630 --> 00:04:28.820
I would never wish to be straight.

00:04:28.820 --> 00:04:30.297
We have so much fun.

00:04:30.297 --> 00:04:32.222
Just my day to day life, being gay,

00:04:32.222 --> 00:04:34.033
I can listen to whatever music I want,

00:04:34.033 --> 00:04:35.980
and it's never a threat to my sexuality.

00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:37.812
- You can be whatever you want to be,

00:04:37.812 --> 00:04:39.580
compared to things that you can't do

00:04:39.580 --> 00:04:41.557
cause maybe that would
be a little too gay.

00:04:41.557 --> 00:04:43.967
- How proud I am of this
person that I've become,

00:04:43.967 --> 00:04:46.603
and how I feel that I am
the most me I've ever been.

00:04:46.603 --> 00:04:49.883
I want that journey for
everyone who is a little gay boy

00:04:49.883 --> 00:04:52.393
or gay girl out there who
doesn't feel accepted.

00:04:52.393 --> 00:04:54.458
- I'm definitely so much
more comfortable being gay

00:04:54.458 --> 00:04:56.486
than I ever have been especially being

00:04:56.486 --> 00:04:58.475
in a big city where it's so accepted.

00:04:58.475 --> 00:05:00.210
I think that there's still a lot of hate.

00:05:00.210 --> 00:05:02.858
A lot of people get gay bashed still,

00:05:02.858 --> 00:05:04.329
and we don't always talk about it.

00:05:04.329 --> 00:05:06.494
I'm trying to, as a gay
man, become much more active

00:05:06.494 --> 00:05:09.848
and talking about that
and putting an end to it.

00:05:09.848 --> 00:05:12.676
(ambient techno music)

00:05:12.676 --> 00:05:15.660
- I think being gay and
overcoming all the struggles

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:17.266
that we have growing up,

00:05:17.266 --> 00:05:19.094
I feel like I'm a lot more empathetic

00:05:19.094 --> 00:05:20.504
to different struggles.

00:05:20.504 --> 00:05:21.759
Even if it doesn't have anything

00:05:21.759 --> 00:05:23.858
to do with being gay, like you can relate.

00:05:23.858 --> 00:05:25.154
- A lot of people are so obsessed

00:05:25.154 --> 00:05:26.673
with other people's relationships

00:05:26.673 --> 00:05:28.027
and like what they're doing

00:05:28.027 --> 00:05:29.706
and they're not even
working on their own selves

00:05:29.706 --> 00:05:31.186
that for me it was kind
of a step to be like,

00:05:31.186 --> 00:05:32.768
"Don't worry about me, like, I'm happy,

00:05:32.768 --> 00:05:35.334
I'm genuinely happy, so like
you should be happy to."

00:05:35.334 --> 00:05:37.290
It's just more accepting
of like other people

00:05:37.290 --> 00:05:39.012
and differences and that it's okay

00:05:39.012 --> 00:05:40.158
that we might not agree on something,

00:05:40.158 --> 00:05:41.670
even as gay people, cause we're both gay,

00:05:41.670 --> 00:05:42.964
but there's probably, we
might have differences

00:05:42.964 --> 00:05:44.636
and that it's okay and
we can talk through them.

00:05:44.636 --> 00:05:46.459
- Being in the gay community
has taught me a lot

00:05:46.459 --> 00:05:48.741
about transparency and acceptance.

00:05:48.741 --> 00:05:50.626
Whoever you are, you can
be totally transparent

00:05:50.626 --> 00:05:52.836
about who you are and we will accept you.

00:05:52.836 --> 00:05:54.760
When you're queer, you have the freedom

00:05:54.760 --> 00:05:56.879
to be as masculine or
as feminine as you want.

00:05:56.879 --> 00:05:59.111
- I think having anything
that's inherently a part

00:05:59.111 --> 00:06:01.744
of who you are that you
have to actively overcome,

00:06:01.744 --> 00:06:03.554
growing up, makes you so strong,

00:06:03.554 --> 00:06:05.165
and I think that that's
what makes me so proud,

00:06:05.165 --> 00:06:07.398
is that I overcame the obstacles

00:06:07.398 --> 00:06:10.010
that came along with
being gay, and that led me

00:06:10.010 --> 00:06:12.039
to a higher place of self-love,

00:06:12.039 --> 00:06:13.376
and that's why I'm so proud of it.

00:06:13.376 --> 00:06:14.959
I'm also just really
proud of this community,

00:06:14.959 --> 00:06:17.586
and everything that it stands for.

00:06:17.586 --> 00:06:20.669
(light techno music)

